{"author":{"id":"249c5793827ca0939286dfdbd6c35d9aabfb778e27ec8eab6c06481033d4a9ab"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791752425,"nonce":"4CCILY9+IbjT7sejr4RzLOkZAXU=","message":"Repinned all xwindow generator/backend/core/clipboard dependencies to eb9ad592375d2b33be1397377008f1718ba7d435 and added xwindow-gamepad only on native targets. build.rs generated the committed Gamepad, GamepadButton, GamepadAxis and GamepadEvent classes; no alternative hand-written loader or binding. The shared API includes 176-byte snapshots and 32-byte event records for reusable fixed-step reads.\n\nThe user requested a version bump and publication of hlwindow's tag. Prepared 0.3.0 in Cargo.toml and haxelib.json, updated the lock, and added libudev-dev to every Linux CI/release header installation because native gilrs requires it.\n\nLocal verification, sequential with one Cargo build worker and the resource guard bypass explicitly requested by the user:\n- Native cdylib build passed (cargo rustc --lib --crate-type cdylib).\n- Clippy all-targets with -D warnings passed.\n- Seven packaging/publisher unit tests passed, using mocks for publication.\n- The xwindow console example and hlwindow Checks example compile with Haxe against the generated bindings.\n- Local Ash release runs the Checks example in default hybrid/game preset: backend available, zero controllers present, invalid controls/rumble rejected, snapshot bytes preserved on failed reads, short event buffers untouched, and 8,192 absent-controller samples allocate zero bytes after warmup. Physical mappings/rumble were not tested without a controller.\n- scripts/build_wasm.sh built the actual 297,943-byte threaded WASI side module. All 303 generated primitive names appear in its exports, including the new Gamepad methods; both generated page modules pass node --check.\n\nUpstream xwindow evidence includes 38 tests, a native stand-in and threaded-wasm compile, generated browser round-trip fixtures with analog/pressed values and reconnect/unmapped cases, three detected mutations and zero allocator-counted snapshot reads. xwindow's chapter documents native/browser support and PlayStation positional labels. Family/glyph/rebinding presentation is tracked in ChimpMonk 3de6572; advanced touchpad/gyro/adaptive-trigger support in xwindow e1e8f21. Native mobile controller input and macOS rumble are explicitly unavailable.\n\nAutomatic approval review rejected pushing the prerequisite xwindow commit to its default branch because the trusted release request specifically named hlwindow. A specific async approval request for that dependency push is pending; publication of the hlwindow tag waits until the pinned revision is fetchable from GitHub. The local build used a process-local Git URL redirect only, with canonical remote sources retained in Cargo.lock.","files":null}]}